IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cema-types`

-- Customs and Excise Management Act 1979 (UK) — GOAL 1: SEIZURE AND
-- CONDEMNATION (s 139(6), Schedule 3 paras 1, 3, 5, 6).
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/ukpga-1979-2.txt.

§ `Goal 1 — seizure and condemnation`

-- Sch 3 para 1 "(1) The Commissioners shall ... give notice of the seizure
-- ... to any person who to their knowledge was at the time of the seizure
-- the owner ... (2) Notice need not be given ... if the seizure was made in
-- the presence of" the offender, an owner (or servant or agent), a person in
-- possession or control, the master or commander, or the driver.
@ref Sch 3 para 1
@export Whether the Commissioners must give notice of seizure under Schedule 3 para 1 to the Customs and Excise Management Act 1979 (UK): an owner is known to them and the seizure was not made in the presence of the offender, an owner (or their servant or agent), a person in possession or control, the master or commander, or the driver. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN s IS A `Seizure facts`  @desc Whether an owner is known and who was present
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `notice of seizure must be given for` s IF
        s's `an owner is known to the Commissioners`
    AND NOT (s's `seized in the presence of the offender, owner, possessor, master or driver`)

-- Sch 3 para 3: a claim "shall, within one month of the date of the notice of
-- seizure or, where no such notice has been served on him, within one month
-- of the date of the seizure, give notice of his claim". Within one month of
-- a date: on or before the corresponding date one month later.
@ref Sch 3 para 3
@export The last day to give notice of claim under Schedule 3 para 3 to the Customs and Excise Management Act 1979 (UK) that a seized thing is not liable to forfeiture: one month after the date of the notice of seizure, or, if none was served, after the date of the seizure (the corresponding date, or the last day of the month if none). DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN s IS A `Seizure facts`  @desc The date of seizure and of any notice of seizure
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day for a notice of claim for` s MEANS
    CONSIDER s's `notice of seizure served on`
    WHEN JUST n  THEN `add months` n 1
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `add months` (s's `seized on`) 1

-- Sch 3 para 5 "If on the expiration of the relevant period under paragraph
-- 3 ... no such notice has been given ..., or if ... any requirement of
-- paragraph 4 ... is not complied with, the thing in question shall be
-- deemed to have been duly condemned as forfeited." Para 6: otherwise the
-- Commissioners "shall take proceedings for the condemnation of that thing
-- by the court".
DECLARE `Condemnation outcome` IS ONE OF
    `deemed condemned as forfeited`
    `the Commissioners must take condemnation proceedings`

@ref Sch 3 paras 3-6
@export What follows a seizure under Schedule 3 to the Customs and Excise Management Act 1979 (UK): the thing is deemed condemned as forfeited if no notice of claim was given within the paragraph 3 period or the claim did not meet paragraph 4; otherwise the Commissioners must take proceedings for its condemnation by the court. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN s IS A `Seizure facts`  @desc The dates of seizure, of any notice of seizure and of any claim, and whether the claim met paragraph 4
GIVETH A `Condemnation outcome`
`the condemnation outcome for` s MEANS
    CONSIDER s's `notice of claim given on`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `deemed condemned as forfeited`
    WHEN JUST c  THEN
        IF       c AT MOST `the last day for a notice of claim for` s
             AND s's `the claim met paragraph 4`
        THEN `the Commissioners must take condemnation proceedings`
        ELSE `deemed condemned as forfeited`
